WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.320 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
If you build for the web you've hit this problem before: your app runs on localhost, but the

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:08.680 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
thing that needs to reach it, a webhook, a client, your phone, is out on the internet

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:09.680 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
and localhost isn't.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:14.080 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
You need a simple way to share what you're building with someone else, and you

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.840 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
can easily do that with viaduct.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:21.160 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
I have a local app here, just running on this machine, in fact on

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:26.960 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
port 8080. It's a little web app, and I want to share it with a friend. To

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:33.820 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
do that I can ask viaduct to map port 8080 and give me a friendly URL I can share.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:39.400 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
It's given me calm-narwhal.viaduct.sh, and this maps directly to the application running

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.840 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
on my machine.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:45.120 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
I can share this with anyone on the internet and they can see the same application.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.440 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
It's a nice, friendly way to quickly share what you're building.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.520 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
viaduct also comes with lots of different features.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:55.280 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
You can turn on the live traffic inspector to see what the app is doing, and interact

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:00.280 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
with it in real time and see what's going on, all from your terminal.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.960 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
It's nice and simple, and free to use.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:03.440 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
There's no sign-up required.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:06.200 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
I built viaduct because I wanted a tunnel small enough to trust.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:11.040 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
It's completely open source, a few thousand lines of Python, easy to read, and the

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.280 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
whole thing can be run on your own box.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.480 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
I'm Adam, and that's viaduct.
